---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DispatchLab from '../../components/DispatchLab.astro';
import PlaygroundCard from '../../components/PlaygroundCard.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const entries = (await getCollection('playground')).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
const more = entries.filter((entry) => entry.id !== 'dispatch-lab');
---

<Layout title="Playground — Vinayak Gupta" description="Small, inspectable experiments. Change an input, follow the outcome, and explore the boundary of a system.">
  <div class="site-shell page-content">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <h1>A small experiment.<br />A clearer mental model.</h1>
      <p>A place to make an idea tangible. Change an input, follow what happens, and look for the boundary.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="lab-layout">
      <div class="lab-intro">
        <h2>When an agent cannot answer.</h2>
        <p>A happy path is only part of a system. What changes when identity is missing, a route is unknown, or the primary agent times out?</p>
        <p>Try removing tenant identity while leaving a fallback available. Notice which rule wins.</p>
        <div class="text-links"><a href="/playground/dispatch-lab">Read the experiment notes &rarr;</a><a href="/work/multi-agent-orchestration-platform">Connect it to real work &rarr;</a></div>
      </div>
      <DispatchLab />
    </section>
    {more.length > 0 && (
      <section class="section-rule">
        <div class="section-top"><h2>More experiments</h2></div>
        <div class="work-gallery">{more.map((entry) => <PlaygroundCard {...entry.data} slug={entry.id} />)}</div>
      </section>
    )}
  </div>
</Layout>
